Spec: SecurityScanners

Purpose:
  Security scanner configuration and execution rules. Scanners are the
  tools that implement security controls. This file defines which
  scanner runs when, how it is configured, and how its output is
  interpreted.

Owns: security\scanners.sdd
Scanners:

  SEC.SECRET:
    truffleHog:
      command: trufflehog --regex --entropy=False .
      on_failure: block
    gitleaks:
      command: gitleaks detect --source .
      on_failure: block
    detect-secrets:
      command: detect-secrets scan
      on_failure: block

  SEC.DEP:
    snyk:
      command: snyk test --severity-threshold=high
      on_failure: block
    npm-audit:
      command: npm audit --audit-level=high
      on_failure: block
    grype:
      command: grype .
      on_failure: block

  SEC.SAST:
    semgrep:
      command: semgrep --config=p/security .
      on_failure: block
    bandit:
      command: bandit -r .
      on_failure: block

  SEC.DAST:
    owasp-zap:
      command: zap-baseline.py -t https://staging.example.com
      on_failure: block
    nuclei:
      command: nuclei -u https://staging.example.com
      on_failure: warn

  SEC.CONTAINER:
    trivy:
      command: trivy image .
      on_failure: block
    docker-scout:
      command: docker scout cves .
      on_failure: block

  SEC.SUPPLY:
    slsa:
      command: slsa-verifier
      on_failure: block
    sigstore:
      command: cosign verify
      on_failure: block

  SEC.IAC:
    checkov:
      command: checkov -d .
      on_failure: block
    tfsec:
      command: tfsec .
      on_failure: block
    kubernetes:
      command: kube-linter lint .
      on_failure: block

ScannerExecution:
  Scanners run at defined points in the pipeline:
    pre-commit: SEC.SECRET (local)
    CI: SEC.DEP, SEC.SAST, SEC.CONTAINER
    post-deploy: SEC.DAST (staging)
    release: SEC.PENTEST (if triggered)

  Scanner results feed into gates.sdd for gate calculation.

ScannerOutput:
  Scanner output MUST be structured:
    scanner
    timestamp
    findings
      severity
      description
      location
      recommendation

  Unstructured output MUST be parsed into this format before
  being used by gates.sdd.

State: +
  Note:
  This file defines the security scanners
  and their execution rules. Scanners are tools that implement security
  controls. This file configures which scanner runs when and how its
  output is interpreted.
